Numeric helpers for roots, absolute values, minima, maxima, powers, and clamps.

Use core.

Publicly, to sqrt given x as a decimal, returning a decimal.
    Call this as "square root of <x>".
    If x < 0.0:
        panic("sqrt of negative number", 23).
    If x == 0.0:
        Give back 0.0.
    Define local guess as a decimal.
    If x >= 1.0:
        Set guess to x * 0.5.
    Else:
        Set guess to 1.0.
    Define local iteration as a whole number.
    While iteration < 24:
        Set guess to 0.5 * (guess + x / guess).
        Add 1 to iteration.
    Give back guess.
Done.

Publicly, to abs_i64 given x as a whole number, returning a whole number.
    If x < 0:
        Give back 0 - x.
    Give back x.
Done.

Publicly, to abs_f64 given x as a decimal, returning a decimal.
    If x == 0.0:
        Give back 0.0.
    If x < 0.0:
        Give back 0.0 - x.
    Give back x.
Done.

Publicly, to min_i64 given a as a whole number, b as a whole number, returning a whole number.
    If a < b:
        Give back a.
    Give back b.
Done.

Publicly, to max_i64 given a as a whole number, b as a whole number, returning a whole number.
    If a > b:
        Give back a.
    Give back b.
Done.

Publicly, to min_f64 given a as a decimal, b as a decimal, returning a decimal.
    If a < b:
        Give back a.
    Give back b.
Done.

Publicly, to max_f64 given a as a decimal, b as a decimal, returning a decimal.
    If a > b:
        Give back a.
    Give back b.
Done.

Publicly, to pow_i64 given base as a whole number, exponent as a whole number, returning a whole number.
    If exponent < 0:
        Give back 0.
    Define local result as a whole number.
    Define local factor as a whole number.
    Define local power as a whole number.
    Set result to 1.
    Set factor to base.
    Set power to exponent.
    While power > 0:
        If power % 2 == 1:
            Set result to result * factor.
        Set factor to factor * factor.
        Set power to power / 2.
    Give back result.
Done.

Publicly, to clamp_i64 given value as a whole number, low as a whole number, high as a whole number, returning a whole number.
    If value < low:
        Give back low.
    If value > high:
        Give back high.
    Give back value.
Done.
